Changes made to the derived files
---------------------------------

All six agents:
  - Frontmatter replaced for Pi (pi-subagents): a one-line description; the
    `model` and `color` fields removed; `tools`, `thinking: high`,
    `systemPromptMode: replace`, `inheritProjectContext: true`,
    `inheritSkills: false`, and `acceptanceRole` added.

  P1  A "Pi runtime notes" section appended to every agent: CLAUDE.md
      references also mean AGENTS.md; the review scope comes from the task,
      falling back to `git diff` and `git diff --cached`; every finding cites
      file:line and evidence; reviewers are read-only (bash for inspection
      only; no edits, commits, pushes, or PR comments). code-simplifier gets
      an edit boundary limited to the task's scope instead.

  P2  silent-failure-hunter: references to project-specific logging and
      error-tracking (logError, logForDebugging, logEvent, constants/errorIds.ts,
      Sentry, Statsig) replaced with the project's own conventions from
      AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, if any. "Special Considerations" made
      project-neutral.

  P3  silent-failure-hunter: "Call out every instance ... no matter how minor"
      changed to report every evidence-backed instance within the review scope
      and no speculative issues.

  P4  code-simplifier: the hard-coded style list (ES modules, `function`
      keyword, explicit return types, React Props types, avoiding try/catch)
      replaced with "follow AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, otherwise match the
      surrounding code". "Recently modified ... in the current session" and
      "operate autonomously and proactively" replaced with "only the scope
      specified in the task, and only when asked".

  P5  code-reviewer: default scope changed from unstaged changes (`git diff`)
      to unstaged and staged changes (`git diff` and `git diff --cached`).

  P6  skills/pr-review/SKILL.md: upstream command kept verbatim; only a
      change notice and the skill `name` field were added to the frontmatter,
      and `allowed-tools` was renamed to Pi tools (Bash, Glob, Grep, Read,
      Task -> bash, find, grep, read, subagent).

